PicoGKRuntime 26.2 (0f26321c) — RC2: call-local unsafe accessors for the
per-point queries. Upstreamable to leap71/PicoGKRuntime; not yet offered.

Applied to vendor/PicoGKRuntime by scripts/fetch-deps.sh after 0001-0008.
Kept as a patch because it modifies dependency source; no flag-level override
exists. Ledger row U31 (upstream/LEDGER.md).

Voxels::bIsInside, ScalarField::bGetValue and VectorField::bGetValue built a
registered ConstAccessor per call, which inserts into and erases from the
tree's tbb::concurrent_hash_map: the audit measured 2.05x on one thread and
3.5x on four with a call-local unsafe accessor, and concurrent queries on one
object collapsed to 0.65 M calls/s on four threads against 4.2 M on one. The
accessor lives for one read, and the caller's shared_ptr keeps the grid alive,
so registration buys nothing. Value-neutral: the same tree reads.
--- a/Source/PicoGKVdbField.h
+++ b/Source/PicoGKVdbField.h
@@ -160,7 +160,10 @@
     bool bGetValue( Vector3 vecPos,
                     float* pfValue)
     {
-        auto oAccess = m_roGrid->getConstAccessor();
+        // A call-local accessor: the unsafe form skips registering with the
+        // tree (an insert into and erase from its concurrent hash map per call).
+        // Reads only, and the caller's shared_ptr keeps the grid alive.
+        auto oAccess = m_roGrid->getConstUnsafeAccessor();
     
         openvdb::Coord xyz( oVoxelSize().iToVoxels(vecPos.X),
                             oVoxelSize().iToVoxels(vecPos.Y),
